== Technical Illustrations ==

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Concept Detailed Technical Illustration''

[[File:Whonix-concept-detailed.jpg|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Concept Detailed Technical Illustration|alt=Diagram: apps in the isolated Whonix-Workstation reach the Internet only through Whonix-Gateway as an anonymous connection; a direct connection is trackable]]

'''Figure:''' ''[https://knowledgesharingtech.com/install-whonix-on-windows-10-step-by-step/ {{project_name_short}} connecting to internet through Tor] by [https://knowledgesharingtech.com/about-me/ Eloy]

[[File:whonix_connection_to_internet.png|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}connecting to internet through Tor] by [https://knowledgesharingtech.com/about-me/ Eloy]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Concept Illustration''

[[File:Whonix-concept-illustration.png|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Concept Illustration|alt=Diagram: on your computer, Whonix traffic is anonymous while a direct connection is not anonymous]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Operating System Design''

[[File:Whonix_concept_refined.jpg|500px|border|Whonix concept refined|alt=Diagram: isolated Whonix-Workstation connects to Whonix-Gateway, which sends torified traffic to the Internet; the host connection is non-torified.]]

'''Figure:''' ''Isolated Routes''

[[File:Stream-isolation-promo.jpg|500px|border|Isolated Routes|alt=Diagram: a laptop sends Thunderbird, Tor Browser and another app over three separate four-hop routes to the web]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Stream Isolation''

[[File:Stream_isolation.1.0.jpg|500px|border|alt=Diagram: Workstation apps with SocksPort setup take separate Tor circuits; apps without it share the TransPort circuit, allowing identity correlation]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Stream Isolation Remodeled''

[[File:WhonixStreamIsolation.jpg|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Stream Isolation Remodeled|alt=Diagram: apps with SocksPort use separate Tor circuits via four relays, while apps without it share one TransPort circuit, causing identity correlation]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Connection With Vanguard Logo''

[[File:Whonix_connection_design_vanguards.jpg|500px|border|Whonix Connection With Vanguard Logo|alt=Diagram: Your Computer connects through four numbered servers to a website, with a Vanguard emblem between servers 1 and 3.]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Whonix Connection Without Vanguard Logo''

[[File:Whonix_connection_design_simple.jpg|500px|border|Whonix Connection Without Vanguard Logo|alt=Diagram: Your Computer connects through four servers in sequence, numbered 1 to 4, to a website.]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Whonix vs VPN Logos In The Middle''

[[File:Whonix_vs_VPNs.jpg|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Whonix vs VPN Logos In The Middle|alt=Comparison: with Whonix, traffic goes through four servers before reaching a website; with a VPN, through a single server]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Whonix vs VPN Logos On The Left''

[[File:WhonixvsVPNontheleft.jpg|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Whonix vs VPN Logos On The Left|alt=Diagram: Whonix sends traffic from your computer through four relays to a website, while a VPN uses one server]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Whonix Connection technical''

[[File:Whonix-4x-tor.jpg|500px|border|{{project_name_short}}Whonix Connection technical|alt=Diagram: your computer connects through four numbered servers in a chain to a website, protecting your IP]]

'''Figure:''' ''{{project_name_short}} Whonix vs VPN technical|{{project_name_short}} Whonix vs VPN technical''

[[File:Whonix-vs-vpn.jpg|500px|border|alt=Diagram: Whonix routes your computer through four relays to a website, while a VPN uses a single server]]

